The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
for (i = fb->format->num_planes; i < ARRAY_SIZE(plane_state->color_plane); i++) {
    plane_state->color_plane[i].offset = ~0xfff;
}
```
Reason:
This updated loop correctly iterates from the number of planes defined in the framebuffer format to the total size of the `color_plane` array, ensuring that all unused color plane offsets are set to `~0xfff`. This guarantees that the `skl_check_main_surface()` function will not use stale offsets, thus maintaining the requirement that the auxiliary distance (AUX_DIST) remains non-negative.

